00:05:33,333 --> 00:05:39,333
A different set of jaws.

2
00:11:06,666 --> 00:11:12,666
The Rocky Horror Picture Show is a comedy, science
fiction, fantasy film directed by Jim Sharman.

3
00:16:40,000 --> 00:16:46,000
After getting a flat tire in the middle of nowhere, newly engaged couple Brad and
Janet encounter the eerie mansion of the flamboyant, seductive Dr.

4
00:22:13,333 --> 00:22:19,333
Frank-N-Furter and a variety of eccentric characters.

5
00:27:46,666 --> 00:27:52,666
Through elaborate dance and rock music, the mad scientist
unveils his latest creation: a perfect, muscular man.

6
00:33:20,000 --> 00:33:26,000
Dr. Frank-N-Furter, played by Tim Curry.

7
00:38:53,333 --> 00:38:59,333
Janet Weiss, played by Susan Sarandon.

8
00:44:26,666 --> 00:44:32,666
Brad Majors, played by Barry Bostwick.

9
00:50:00,000 --> 00:50:06,000
Riff Raff, played by Richard O'Brien.

10
00:55:33,333 --> 00:55:39,333
Magenta, played by Patricia Quinn.

11
01:01:06,666 --> 01:01:12,666
Columbia, played by Nell Campbell.

12
01:06:40,000 --> 01:06:46,000
The Rocky Horror Picture Show is the original soundtrack album to the 1975 film The Rocky
Horror Picture Show, an adaptation of the 1973 musical The Rocky Horror Show.

13
01:12:13,333 --> 01:12:19,333
The 1975 soundtrack album was released by Ode
Records and produced by Richard Hartley.

14
01:17:46,666 --> 01:17:52,666
It should not be confused with The Rocky Horror Show album, a recording of the
theatrical music by Tim Curry and the original cast from The Roxy Theatre.

15
01:23:20,000 --> 01:23:26,000
The latter album was released in 1974, also by Ode Records.

16
01:28:53,333 --> 01:28:59,333
The film explores themes of sexual identity, rock 'n'
roll, transvestism, time warp, transylvania.

17
01:34:26,666 --> 01:34:32,666
The tone is lighthearted and dark and thought_provoking.
